	(text "NIBBLE CARD CLOCK: RC oscillator with a speed knob, RUN/STEP switch, halt, power-on reset"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "917071ef-7711-4c9a-b583-08b62811e17f")
	)
	(text "16 transistors, 20 resistors, 2 LEDs, one pot, one switch, one jumper, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nRUN: the switch puts 10k from +5V on CLK and the oscillator pulls CLK low for half of each cycle, or for as long as HLT is high.\nSTEP: the switch is open and the pull-down transistor is held off; the front panel's CLK button owns the line, one edge per press.\nSpeed: a Schmitt-trigger RC oscillator, 100k + the pot from SA to X, 47n on X: about 500 Hz down to 40 Hz; the SLOW jumper adds 2.2u for 10 Hz down to 0.8 Hz.\nPower-on reset: 2.2 uF charging through 100k into a Schmitt trigger holds RST high for a tenth of a second after power-up, so the machine starts at address 0 without touching the panel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a98a3867-3900-400c-a641-7b450f90c571")
	)
	(text "OSCILLATOR BUFFERS: SA = NOT VD2 (VD2 is Q2's drain, high while X is above the trip point) with a 4.7k pull-up: SA charges and discharges X through R.  SB = NOT SA is the clock phase"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "833017bb-683e-49bf-81d9-e184f9a91573")
	)
